      "created_at": "2016-07-19T02:57:10Z",
      "updated_at": "2016-07-19T02:57:10Z",
      "body": "This patch fixes errors reported by GCC’s undefined behaviour sanitizer about calling functions with a null pointer:\r\n\r\n./configure CC=\"gcc -fsanitize=undefined\"\r\n\r\nUsing bpo-22605 as a precedent, I propose to avoid calling memcpy() and memmove() for zero-length copies when there may be a null pointer.",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
      "reactions": {
